+# Specification: Sustained $\ge 30\text{ tok/s}$ Speculative Generation up to 16k Context
+
+## 1. Goal
+
+Achieve sustained $\ge 30.0\text{ tok/s}$ token generation throughput on Gemma 4 31B (`Gxma-repacked`, EXL3 ~3 bpw, 12.055 GB weights) across contexts up to 16,384 tokens on Apple M4 Pro (20 GPU cores, 24 GiB unified RAM, 273 GB/s peak memory bus). The engine automatically uses the resident assistant drafter (`~/.omlx/models/mlx-community/gemma-4-31B-it-qat-assistant-4bit`) by default with verify-gated math ensuring zero quality loss.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Non-goals and Restrictions
+
+- **No KV cache quantization**: Full and sliding KV caches remain unquantized in 16-bit float formats (fp16/bf16).
+- **No quality degradation**: Speculative execution must be mathematically verify-gated against the target model's output distribution (greedy identical at temperature 0, exact distribution sampling for temperature > 0).
+- **No Python**: Pure Rust and raw Metal Shading Language (MSL).
+- **No unified memory overflow**: Peak memory footprint must strictly remain under 14 GiB to eliminate OS memory swapping.
+- **Single-user chat focus**: Hot path avoids multi-tenant overhead or batching serialization costs.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Requirements
+
+1. **R1: Default Drafter Auto-Detection & Loading**
+   - Automatically detect and load `~/.omlx/models/mlx-community/gemma-4-31B-it-qat-assistant-4bit` if present, unless explicitly disabled with `--no-drafter` or overridden with `--drafter <path>`.
+2. **R2: Speculative Generation Loop Integration (`generate_speculative`)**
+   - Wire the validated drafter forward pass and target verification into the core engine generation entry points (`generate_speculative` and `generate_gpu`).
+   - Implement cache rollback on draft rejection so KV cache positions and sequence history remain monotonic and exact.
+3. **R3: Batched Verification Over Draft Horizon ($K \in [3, 5]$)**
+   - Draft $K$ tokens via fast drafter execution ($< 2\text{ ms}$ total) against shared KV layers 58 & 59.
+   - Run verification with minimal host dispatch overhead, streaming target weights once per candidate sequence.
+4. **R4: Sustained $\ge 30\text{ tok/s}$ Across Contexts up to 16k**
+   - Benchmark generation at 1k, 4k, 8k, and 16k context lengths, confirming throughput meets or exceeds $30.0\text{ tok/s}$.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Acceptance Criteria
+
+- All bit-exact regression tests pass (`live_kernel_bit_exact`, `decode_matvec_golden`, `repacked_golden`, `norm_rope_qkv_bit_exact`).
+- `drafter_load` and `drafter_forward` tests pass.
+- End-to-end benchmark `./target/release/kaplumba --model ~/.kaplumba/models/Gxma-repacked --prompt "..." --max-new-tokens 64 --metrics` achieves $\ge 30.0\text{ tok/s}$ sustained throughput.
+- Sabotage verification: perturbing token acceptance logic produces immediate diagnosable test failures.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Open Questions
+
+*(None. All requirements, drafter weights, and hardware metrics empirically confirmed.)*
