+# plan — `spec/decode-alu-flash-20tok`
+
+## 1. Architecture and Data Flow
+
+```
+[Prompt Tokens / In-Flight Token]
+              │
+              ▼
+    [Embedding Lookup & Input Norm]
+              │
+              ▼
+   ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+   │ Layer Loop (60 Layers)                                 │
+   │                                                        │
+   │ 1. Attention Projections (GEMV):                       │
+   │    - Sliding (50 layers): fused3_2col (q, k, v)        │
+   │    - Full (10 layers):    fused2_2col (q, k)           │
+   │    ==> Unrolled 4-deep (_tl4) at 240 GB/s              │
+   │                                                        │
+   │ 2. Attention Core:                                     │
+   │    - Sliding (50 layers): 1024-token bounded ring      │
+   │      (Key count clamped <= 1024, constant O(1))        │
+   │    - Full (10 layers): 2-pass FlashDecode              │
+   │      (256-key threadgroup chunks across 20 cores)      │
+   │                                                        │
+   │ 3. Output Projection: o_proj_colmajor_2col_sk2         │
+   │    ==> Unrolled 4-deep (_tl4) at 240 GB/s              │
+   │                                                        │
+   │ 4. MLP Block (GEMV):                                   │
+   │    - gate_up_fused2_2col (gate + up + GeLU)            │
+   │    - down_proj_colmajor_2col_sk2                       │
+   │    ==> Unrolled 4-deep (_tl4) at 240 GB/s              │
+   │                                                        │
+   │ 5. Residual Add & Norm Pipeline (fused)                │
+   └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+              │
+              ▼
+    [lm_head Proj (6 bpw, 257 GB/s)]
+              │
+              ▼
+    [Device-Side Top-K / Draw (Pipelined)]
+```
+
+---
+
+## 2. File / Module Touchpoints
+
+### 2.1 `crates/kernels/src/linear_repacked.metal`
+- **Current Behavior**:
+  - `linear_gemv_ishizuki_k3_fused2_2col` (line 434): unrolled 2-deep along K (`SG * 2u`), then a 1-deep remainder loop. Runs at ~203 GB/s.
+  - `linear_gemv_ishizuki_k3_fused3_2col` (line 1506): unrolled 2-deep along K. Runs at ~200 GB/s.
+  - `linear_gemv_ishizuki_k3_colmajor_2col_sk2` (line 2549): unrolled 2-deep along K. Runs at ~202 GB/s.
+- **Intended Change**:
+  - Implement `_tl4` (4-deep tile-loop unroll with step `SG * 4u`) across all 3 kernels.
+  - Keep tile assignment and lane accumulation order identical to maintain exact IEEE floating-point summation order.
+  - Do NOT introduce threadgroup barriers (`_u4` mistake).
+
+### 2.2 `crates/kernels/src/attention.metal` & `crates/engine/src/gpu_cache.rs`
+- **Current Behavior**:
+  - In `attention.metal:54`, the kernel loop tests `params.window != 0u && query_position - key_position >= params.window`.
+  - In split decode, `range_end` partitions the full `key_count`.
+- **Intended Change**:
+  - On sliding layers, ensure that `key_count` passed to attention is strictly `min(next_position, 1024)`, and indexing wraps into the circular ring buffer.
+  - For full layers, apply 2-pass FlashDecode with 256-key block splits (`b = (((N + 255) / 256 + 31) / 32) * 32`) matching omlx 0.7.0.
+
+### 2.3 `crates/kernels/src/linear.metal`
+- **Current Behavior**:
+  - `linear_input_transform` runs separately before GEMVs, dispatching 60 extra kernels per token.
+- **Intended Change**:
+  - Fuse Hadamard transform computation directly into GEMV `x` loads, eliminating 60 dispatches and activation round-trips.
+
+### 2.4 `crates/engine/src/chat.rs`
+- **Current Behavior**:
+  - Gates pipelining on `self.greedy`.
+- **Intended Change**:
+  - Allow pipelining when `device_sampler_supported(config)` is true.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Sequencing and Dependencies
+
+```
+T0: Baseline Pinning & Verification
+ └── T1: Tile-Loop 4-Deep Unroll (_tl4) in linear_repacked.metal
+      └── T2: Bit-Exactness & Golden Tests Verification
+           └── T3: Sliding Attention 1024-Key Ring Bounding
+                └── T4: Full Attention 2-Pass FlashDecode Optimization
+                     └── T5: Input Transform Hadamard Fusion
+                          └── T6: Device Sampler Pipelining
+                               └── T7: End-to-End Interleaved A/B Benchmarks
+```
+
+---
+
+## 4. Risks and Fallbacks
+
+1. **Register Spilling in `_tl4` Unroll**:
+   - *Risk*: An unroll factor of 4 increases register pressure per thread, which could reduce occupancy.
+   - *Mitigation*: The arithmetic intensity per tile is small, and `arm_decode_u4` in `alu_boost.rs` proved zero register spilling on M4 Pro. If any kernel spills, fallback to unrolling 2 pairs of contiguous tiles.
+2. **Bit-Exact Divergence**:
+   - *Risk*: Any reordering of floating-point accumulations changes the output by 1 ULP.
+   - *Mitigation*: Sabotage-tested verification on every step; enforce identical accumulation sequences.
+3. **Contention on Shared GPU**:
+   - *Risk*: Concurrency during testing invalidates benchmark timings.
+   - *Mitigation*: Strict enforcement of `scripts/gpuq try --` with 16 interleaved A/B pairs.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Requirement Mapping
+
+| Requirement | Tasks | Verification Method |
+|---|---|---|
+| R1 (`_tl4` unroll) | T1, T2 | `repacked_golden` bit-exact test + GEMV bandwidth probe |
+| R2 (constant shift) | T1 | Inspection of compiled Metal shader assembly + unit tests |
+| R3 (sliding bounding) | T3 | Attention microbenchmark across 1k, 4k, 16k context |
+| R4 (omlx FlashDecode) | T4 | Full attention layer execution timing at 16k context |
+| R5 (Hadamard fusion) | T5 | Dispatch count verification + bit-exact activations |
+| R6 (sampler pipeline) | T6 | `perf_probe_host_ops` test + wall-clock timing |
+| R7 (sabotage coverage) | T2, T7 | Intentional perturbation tests confirming failure |
