+# spec/decode-alu-flash-20tok — ALU Boost & Constant-Time Decode Attention to Reach 20 tok/s
+
+## 1. Goal
+
+Achieve steady-state single-token autoregressive decode throughput of **$\ge 18.5\text{--}20.0\text{ tok/s}$** ($\le 50.0\text{--}54.0\text{ ms/token}$) for Gemma 4 31B (`Gxma-repacked`, EXL3 ~3.0 bpw) on Apple M4 Pro (20 GPU cores, 24 GiB unified RAM, 273 GB/s peak wire bandwidth). This is accomplished by boosting the 3 bpw GEMV dequantization ALU from ~200 GB/s to its physical copy ceiling of **245–250 GB/s** via tile loop unrolling (`_tl4`), while maintaining constant-time decode attention across context lengths up to 16k tokens by bounding the 50 sliding-window layers to their 1024-token active ring and adopting omlx 0.7.0's 2-pass parallel block-tiled FlashDecode for the 10 full layers. Output must remain **100% bit-exact greedy generation** against the golden baseline.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Non-Goals / Restrictions
+
+1. **No Quality Loss / Bit-Exact Invariant:**
+   Greedy text generation at temperature 0 must remain 100% bit-exact against the reference (`repacked_golden`, `live_kernel_bit_exact`). Zero numeric drift on greedy outputs.
+2. **No KV Cache Quantization:**
+   KV states remain FP16 (or BF16). No INT8/INT4/FP8 quantization of KV caches (standing project constraint `AGENTS.md §8`).
+3. **Pure Forward First:**
+   This spec focuses entirely on pure autoregressive forward acceleration. It does not introduce lossy approximations, prompt pruning, or untested drafters.
+4. **Single-User Target & Memory Footprint:**
+   Single-user chat target only. Resident GPU memory footprint must remain under the 16.5 GiB physical budget on the 24 GiB unified memory machine. Zero swap activity.
+5. **GPU Access Discipline:**
+   Every test and benchmark must use `scripts/gpuq try -- <cmd>`. Never run concurrent model processes or sit in blocking waits (`AGENTS.md §10`).
+6. **No Python on Engine Hot Path:**
+   Product and inference engine code is pure Rust + raw Metal shaders (`AGENTS.md §8`).
+
+---
+
+## 3. Requirements
+
+- **R1 — Tile-Loop 4-Deep Unroll (`_tl4`):**
+  Unroll the $16 \times 16$ tile loop 4-deep in the live decode GEMV kernels (`linear_gemv_ishizuki_k3_fused2_2col`, `linear_gemv_ishizuki_k3_fused3_2col`, `linear_gemv_ishizuki_k3_colmajor_2col_sk2`) in `crates/kernels/src/linear_repacked.metal`. Preserve exact per-thread tile assignment and accumulation order to ensure bit-exact float summation without adding threadgroup synchronization barriers.
+- **R2 — Dynamic Barrel Shift Optimization:**
+  Eliminate variable dynamic 64-bit barrel shifts `(A >> (64 - rad))` in all active decode paths by using pre-masked 32-bit words with compile-time constant shift amounts (`extract_v_mcg_32`).
+- **R3 — Strict 1024-Token Bounding for 50 Sliding Layers:**
+  Ensure the 50 sliding-window attention layers (`window = 1024`) strictly iterate only over the active $\le 1024$ keys in their ring buffer, preventing stale ring slot checks or loop iterations beyond 1024 keys regardless of total conversation sequence length.
+- **R4 — omlx-Style 2-Pass Block-Tiled FlashDecode for 10 Full Layers:**
+  Adopt omlx 0.7.0's 2-pass parallel block-tiled flash decode architecture (`blocks = min(256, (N + 255) / 256)`) with 256-key threadgroup chunks on the 10 full attention layers, parallelizing across the 20 M4 Pro cores to keep full attention latency bounded at $\le 2\text{ ms}$ at 16k context.
+- **R5 — Input Transform Hadamard Fusion:**
+  Fuse `linear_input_transform` directly into the GEMV activation load path (`x`), eliminating 60 kernel dispatches per token and 0.65 MB of intermediate activation round-trips.
+- **R6 — Device Sampler Non-Blocking Pipeline:**
+  Open the pipelined decode loop to sampling when `device_sampler_supported(config)` is true, eliminating the host-side synchronization barrier on non-greedy paths.
+- **R7 — Sabotage-Verified Coverage:**
+  Every modified kernel path must be verified against sabotage (§3.4 of `AGENTS.md`): deliberately modify the computation, confirm the diagnostic test fails with a clear message, and revert.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Acceptance Criteria
+
+1. **AC1: Sustained Decode Throughput:**
+   - Short-to-medium context ($\le 2\text{k}$ tokens): $\ge 18.5\text{ tok/s}$ sustained (median of $\ge 16$ interleaved paired runs).
+   - Long context ($16\text{k}$ tokens): $\ge 17.0\text{--}18.0\text{ tok/s}$ sustained (pure decode, flat attention).
+2. **AC2: 100% Bit-Exact Greedy Generation:**
+   Greedy output on standard test prompts ("Explain the theory of relativity...", "The capital of France is Paris.") produces identical token IDs and identical SHA-256 hashes compared to the golden baseline.
+3. **AC3: GEMV Streaming Bandwidth:**
+   Live layer GEMVs sustain $\ge 225\text{--}240\text{ GB/s}$ of effective DRAM read bandwidth on Apple M4 Pro (up from the current ~200 GB/s baseline).
+4. **AC4: Flat Attention Latency:**
+   Attention time across all 60 layers remains $\le 6.0\text{ ms}$ total at 16k context.
+5. **AC5: Test Suite & Sabotage:**
+   All engine and kernel unit tests pass (`cargo test -p kaplumba-engine --test repacked_golden`, `live_kernel_bit_exact`, `fused_bit_exact`). Sabotage tests documented with exact failure messages.
+6. **AC6: Zero Swap Activity:**
+   Physical memory footprint remains $\le 16.5\text{ GiB}$ resident with 0 MiB swap.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Open Questions
+
+*(None. All design requirements clarified and confirmed.)*
