+# Specification: Pure Autoregressive Decode $\ge 20\text{ tok/s}$
+
+## 1. Goal
+
+Achieve sustained $\ge 20.0\text{ tok/s}$ pure autoregressive token generation on Gemma 4 31B (`Gxma-repacked`, EXL3 ~3 bpw, 12.055 GB weights) on Apple M4 Pro (20 GPU cores, 24 GiB unified RAM, 273 GB/s peak bus) under standard sampling conditions (`temperature = 1.0`, `top_k = 64`).
+
+---
+
+## 2. Non-goals and Restrictions
+
+- **No KV cache quantization**: KV states remain in fp16/bf16 with zero precision degradation.
+- **No speculative decoding or prompt lookup**: Generation must be pure autoregressive forward passes on the primary 31B model.
+- **No quality loss**: All GEMV, dequantization, normalization, and attention math must remain bit-exact or numerically faithful.
+- **No Python**: All changes are in Rust and Metal Shading Language (MSL).
+- **No memory regressions**: Unified memory footprint must remain under 14 GiB to avoid swapping.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Requirements
+
+1. **R1: Bit-Exact EXL3 4-Way Pipelining**: Interleave dequantization math in the inner GEMV loop to eliminate integer dependency stalls, boosting GEMV throughput towards $\ge 240\text{ GB/s}$.
+2. **R2: Multi-Core Utilization on Finalize / Norms**: Eliminate 1-threadgroup dispatches in `linear.rs` / `linear.metal` by widening grids to wave-sized threadgroup counts (e.g., 42–168 threadgroups), reducing per-dispatch overhead from 4.6 µs to 0.7 µs.
+3. **R3: Command Buffer & Queue Optimization**: Streamline command buffer submission and pipeline rolling to eliminate dispatch bubbles between decoder layers.
+4. **R4: End-to-End Performance**: Sustain $\ge 20.0\text{ tok/s}$ during interactive and benchmark generation runs.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Acceptance Criteria
+
+- `cargo test -p kaplumba-engine --test live_kernel_bit_exact` passes with 0 mismatches.
+- `cargo test -p kaplumba-engine --test decode_matvec_golden` passes.
+- `scripts/gpuq run -- ./target/release/kaplumba --model ~/.kaplumba/models/Gxma-repacked --prompt "Explain the theory of relativity." --max-new-tokens 64 --temperature 1.0 --metrics` achieves $\ge 20.0\text{ tok/s}$.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Open Questions
+
+*(None. All hardware requirements and constraints empirically verified.)*
